IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — GOAL 3 (PART): COMMENCEMENT.
--
--   "On what day does the benefit commence after the stand-down?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_32.txt — ss 313, 316.

§ `Commencement`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- s 316 "(1) A benefit ... is subject to a stand-down period that— (a) starts
-- on the later of— (i) the date on which the person became entitled to the
-- benefit; and (ii) if, before the person applied for the benefit, the
-- person's employment terminated ..., the day after the date on which the
-- person's employment ceased; and (b) is calculated under regulations made
-- under section 440."
@ref s 316(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Commencement facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the stand-down starts for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER (IF c's `employment terminated, or notice given, before applying` THEN c's `employment ceased on` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN IF `the day` 1 `days after` ceased GREATER THAN entitled THEN `the day` 1 `days after` ceased ELSE entitled
    WHEN NOTHING THEN entitled
    WHERE
        entitled MEANS c's `became entitled on`

-- s 316 "(2) The benefit commences on the day after the stand-down period ends
-- if the application for the benefit is received within 28 days after the
-- date on which the person becomes entitled to the benefit, and the benefit
-- is— (a) sole parent support; or (b) a supported living payment; or (c)
-- jobseeker support granted on the ground of health condition, injury, or
-- disability; or (d) [jobseeker support to a sole parent, or under s 30(e)];
-- or (e) [jobseeker support after recently losing a partner's support] ...
-- (3) If the benefit is not one specified in subsection (2)(a) to (g), the
-- benefit commences on the later of the following days: (a) the day after the
-- stand-down period ends: (b) the day on which the application for the
-- benefit is received." For a listed benefit applied for more than 28 days
-- after entitlement the section gives no rule — subsection (3) covers only
-- benefits not listed — so the encoding refuses (changed after the
-- independent pass; fork F1). A stand-down of n days starting on day S ends
-- on day S + n − 1.
@ref ss 313, 316(1)-(3)
@export The day a main benefit commences under s 316 of the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ): the stand-down (its length set by regulations) runs from the later of entitlement and the day after employment ended; sole parent support, the supported living payment and the listed kinds of jobseeker support start the day after it ends if applied for within 28 days of entitlement; any other benefit starts on the later of that day and the day the application is received; a listed benefit applied for later than 28 days is refused, as s 316 gives no rule for it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Main benefit`  @desc The benefit
      c IS A `Commencement facts`  @desc Entitlement, any end of employment, the application date, the stand-down length, and whether jobseeker support is of a kind in s 316(2)(d)-(e)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the benefit commences, benefit` b `, facts` c MEANS
    IF   listed
    THEN IF   c's `application received on` AT MOST `the day` 28 `days after` (c's `became entitled on`)
         THEN afterStandDown
         ELSE `s 316 gives no commencement rule for a listed benefit applied for more than 28 days after entitlement`
    ELSE IF afterStandDown GREATER THAN c's `application received on` THEN afterStandDown ELSE c's `application received on`
    WHERE
        afterStandDown MEANS `the day` (c's `stand-down period, in days`) `days after` (`the day the stand-down starts for` c)
        listed MEANS
               NOT b EQUALS `jobseeker support`
            OR c's `jobseeker support of a kind in s 316(2)(d)-(e)`

`s 316 gives no commencement rule for a listed benefit applied for more than 28 days after entitlement` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 316(2) applies only to an application within 28 days, and s 316(3) only to benefits not listed in s 316(2)"
